VPOS FTC - CURRENT RELEASE CHANGES
==================================
Release: 0.1.50 (unreleased)
Previous published release: 0.1.44 / 47222001t044
Status: Unreleased
Scope: Changes introduced after the previous published release

RELEASE HIGHLIGHTS
------------------
- Enable Kenya invoice fiscalization with KES currency and supported payment tenders.
- Support Kenya product registration using the dedicated product batch contract.
- Seed Kenya-compliant fuel product codes and tax defaults on PSS config.xml import.
- Prevent unsaved product classification selections from resetting in the edit form.
- Display report transaction timestamps as readable local date and time.
- Maintain structured, traceable software release notes.

DETAILED CHANGES
----------------
Kenya fiscalization and product registration
- Serialize Kenya invoices with Currency and Payment.Tenders in the expected
  proxy-facing format (872ed257, e8c1b675).
- Provide Kenya payment options and normalize cash, credit, cheque, card,
  mobile money and other tender identifiers (be2b0594, 2dfbda0d).
- Introduce typed payment tender contracts and expand payment form validation
  for Kenya while retaining Tanzania behavior (e3bd5b48, 5d51606b).
- Add Kenya-specific product registration mapping using products[] with the
  expected product identification, unit, currency, tax and hazard fields
  (f687b4de, 7c2f1df0).
- Fix Kenya fiscalization payment field typing (dc504ae3, 6ca4a1f3).

PSS XML import and product administration
- Seed Kenya product type 2, tax code B, KES and fuel packaging TY on PSS
  config.xml import; preserve existing classification data where applicable
  (4a45e644, 5a730f6e, 7d95552f).
- Apply provided Petrol 93, Petrol 95 and Diesel 50 product class defaults
  to matching imported grades, including generic Petrol/Diesel grade names
  (47f34c53).
- Pass imported product class/type values through to the proxy instead of
  null values (4a45e644).
- Stabilize initial edit form values so product class/type selections are not
  reset by rerenders before saving (951a923c).
- Add regression coverage for Kenya PSS import defaults (f1eca1e7).

Reporting and usability
- Display transaction timestamps on the Reports page in readable local date
  and time instead of raw UTC values (aab54214).

Documentation and maintenance
- Restore historical package change records (9a7090bb).
- Organize and standardize published release archive entries (232f869e, 523ab68e).
- Synchronize the application manifest and lockfile at version 0.1.50.

RELEASE NOTES
-------------
This is the active unpublished 0.1.50 changelog, not a publication record.
The previous published release recorded in the changelog archive is 0.1.44.
Kenya fuel class values are import defaults based on the supplied product
registration examples; verify site-specific classifications and tax settings
before production deployment. This changelog does not imply full CI validation.
The packaging tool generates the DOMS release ID during build and archives
the current changelog only when the release is published.
